From b92b5ef82448ee80bd4a83329c2ffe8861beafe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Aldea <andrei1998@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:13:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] board: beagleplay: enable IT66121 HDMI boot menu

Add a video-only ITE IT66121 bridge driver with HPD, EDID, fallback timing, RGB input, and AFE setup. Teach TIDSS to activate its AM625 DPI pipeline through a video bridge and use display_timing pixel clocks in Hz.

Route TOBI output to both serial and vidconsole so a missing display never removes UART access.

Show the packaged TI logo for three seconds before opening the TOBI menu, then
leave the menu available for ten seconds. Try loading the logo from SD first and
eMMC second so a missing boot partition does not interrupt boot. Use a dark
console theme so the boot menu is white-on-black.

Teach the TIDSS graph walker that terminal sinks such as an HDMI connector use
a singular port node. Without this, the valid BeaglePlay DPI pipeline is
rejected before the IT66121 driver can probe.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [includes TOBI-specific console policy]

Signed-off-by: Andrei Aldea <andrei1998@gmail.com>
---
 board/beagle/beagleplay/tobi.env       |   9 +-
 board/beagle/beagleplay/beagleplay.c   |  24 ++
 configs/am62x_beagleplay_a53_defconfig |  19 +-
 drivers/video/bridge/Kconfig           |  11 +
 drivers/video/bridge/Makefile          |   1 +
 drivers/video/bridge/ite-it66121.c     | 545 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/video/tidss/tidss_drv.c        | 116 ++++--
 drivers/video/tidss/tidss_drv.h        |   1 +
 8 files changed, 693 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/video/bridge/ite-it66121.c

